{{GM|$Craft|$Clothes & Equipment|$Tools|$Axes|$Stone Axe}}

The Stone Axe is an early game tool, commonly the first tool to be crafted. It counts as an "axe" a "sharp tool" and a "weapon."

An axe is required to cut a [[log]] into [[Block of Wood|blocks]]. Different types of logs provide different amounts of blocks, see more [[Tree|here]]. Blocks can also be further split into [[branch]]es. Enables [[Mining]].

Sharp tools enable actions like flaying, butchering, shearing. Quality of skins, raw meats, [[intestines]], and [[entrails]] will be [[Hardcap]]ped by the sharp tool quality.

It increases the speed of destroying objects (+1 damage when destroying.)

==Quality==

The quality of a stone axe is the average of materials used, and is [[Softcap|softcapped]] by [[Intelligence]] and [[Survival]].

Stone axe can be spiralled up by mining better stone and using better stone axes to split better sticks from blocks to create a higher quality axe, then repeating the process until diminishing returns.

==Upgrades==

[[Tinker's Throwing Axe]] has higher mining strength and can be thrown.

[[Metal Axe]], increase yield of [[Block of Wood|blocks]] by + ~25% and increase chopping speed.

[[Woodsman's Axe]] chopping speed is higher than of Metal Axe.